test(security): prove a high-severity CodeQL finding blocks a merge

Not for merging. Throwaway probe; delete the branch once observed.

The repo's `code_scanning` ruleset rule names CodeQL at
security=high_or_higher and alerts=errors, and has never had a qualifying
alert to act on -- every CodeQL alert in this repo's history is one rule,
actions/missing-workflow-permissions, at medium/warning, below both
thresholds. So "it has never blocked anything" and "it does not work"
have been indistinguishable from the outside.

Adds one package with two deliberate findings, both security-severity 7.5:

  go/weak-cryptographic-algorithm  local query, fires regardless of the
                                   stdlib extraction gap -- the reliable half
  go/path-injection                taint-tracked, and problem.severity error,
                                   so it is the only half that also exercises
                                   the alerts=errors threshold

Branched from main rather than from ci/codeql-extraction-visibility on
purpose: a CodeQL job that fails for its own reasons would block the merge
too and prove nothing about this rule.

Carries //nolint:gosec on three lines. gosec flags the same constructs
(G501, G304, G705), and a red golangci-lint would confound the result --
the point is to isolate what the code_scanning rule does on its own.

